codex
Because leaderboard mode regenerates weights for every timed iteration, the current weight transpose/cache path is mostly a timed cost rather than a reusable optimization. I’m going to test kernels that consume the original `[hidden, dim]` weights directly, avoiding per-run transpose allocations.
codex
I’m making a scoped edit now: a single Triton pack kernel will transpose and cast the five projection weights into a reusable FP16 workspace in one launch. This keeps the projection kernel’s coalesced weight layout while removing five PyTorch transpose/cast allocations from timed leaderboard iterations.
apply patch
